Subject: [RFC PATCH net-next 0/2] net: cake timer slack, bridge ARP early return

STATUS: HOLD.  Neither patch has a runtime measurement yet, and patch 1
needs an iproute2 counterpart.  Do not post until the tests listed in
TESTS-TO-RUN.md have been run.  The text below is written for posting
once they have.

Two independent changes on per-packet paths:

1. sch_cake: a TCA_CAKE_TIMER_SLACK attribute like sch_fq's.  The
   default of 0 keeps the current behaviour.
2. bridge: br_do_proxy_suppress_arp() returns early when no port has
   proxy ARP or neighbour suppression.

  #  summary                        impact                   evidence
  1  cake timer slack attribute     low: only when set       not tested
  2  bridge ARP early return        low: ARP on plain        not tested
                                    bridges

Testing:
- Each commit builds the touched objects (sch_cake.o,
  br_arp_nd_proxy.o, br_if.o, br_input.o, br_netlink.o, br_sysfs_if.o)
  with W=1 and no warnings on x86_64.
- checkpatch.pl --strict is clean apart from the missing Signed-off-by.
- pahole: struct cake_sched_config goes from 56 to 64 bytes.
- Generated code, built kernel: cake_dequeue() 868 -> 871 instructions;
  br_do_proxy_suppress_arp() 301 -> 306 (a 5-instruction early return).

Not tested:
- Neither patch has been measured or run.
- There is no iproute2 support for TCA_CAKE_TIMER_SLACK.
- No allyesconfig/allmodconfig builds, no sparse, no selftests.
- The series is against v7.3-rc3 (518e5b794c06), not net-next.

Tool assistance: the changes, changelogs and measurements in this series
were produced with Claude (Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5) as a coding
assistant.  It was asked to find and fix performance problems in the
networking forwarding path and to measure them.  Each patch carries an
Assisted-by tag.

